NPZSee for VS Code 0.2.0
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

NPZSee-vscode is the independently maintained VS Code continuation of the
npzview Rust rewrite and its initial VS Code prototype. It retains the Rust data
core and adds general multidimensional-array copy, inline Table details, six
interface languages, Arabic RTL and VS Code distribution/release workflows.

npzview is an independently named Rust rewrite derived from and inspired by
npyquick. It is a continuation of that project's array-viewing concepts and
behavior, rather than a claim that all design and provenance are unrelated.

Upstream: https://github.com/LiukDiihMieu/npyquick
Upstream base commit: 6be16fd (2026 source snapshot).
Upstream copyright: Copyright (C) 2026 LiukDiihMieu.
Rust rewrite and modifications: Copyright (C) 2026 npzview contributors.

Modifications include native Rust data loading and rendering, background jobs,
array sidebar, table-first hierarchy and JSON navigation, histogram area fill,
packaging, portability fixes, and a separate name. See CHANGELOG.md and agent.md.

The npzview-vscode source copy additionally separates a headless Rust backend
from VS Code integration and a TypeScript/JavaScript webview. Native data parsing,
mapped storage, slicing, waveform decimation and statistical computation remain
in Rust. The VS Code extension is a separate project and distribution.

